}\\times {A}_{4\\times 5}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{5\\times 5}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $5$ distinct singular values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429230 #edb/ref 1030 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429230 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account linear: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: linear=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/linear-frequency-estimates.json, pair 3819->991. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429230 #edb/ref 1036 #edb/ref 17592186048775 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186434790 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186434791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434790 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186434792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434790 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186434793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434790 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186434794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434790 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186434795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434790 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434790 #edb/ref 1045 "Computing the Singular Values of a Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434790 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186434793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434790 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434790 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 1